## Component Architecture

### Base Components (Always Use These)

**DO NOT create new modules. All components should be standalone.**

Use these base components for all pages:

1. **ItemList** ([src/app/components/item-list/item-list-component.ts](mdc:src/app/components/item-list/item-list-component.ts))

   - For all list/table pages
   - Handles pagination, sorting, search
   - Configure with `ItemListConfig`

2. **ItemDetail** ([src/app/components/item/detail/item-detail-component.ts](mdc:src/app/components/item/detail/item-detail-component.ts))

   - For all detail/edit forms
   - Handles CRUD operations
   - Configure with `ItemDetailConfig`

3. **Dashboard** ([src/app/components/dashboard/dashboard-component.ts](mdc:src/app/components/dashboard/dashboard-component.ts))
   - For all dashboard pages
   - Handles widgets, charts, KPIs
   - Configure with `DashboardConfig`

### Page Types

#### List Pages

- Use `ItemListComponent` with `ItemListConfig`
- Example: User list, project list, client list
- Must include pagination with skip/take
- Configure columns with: field, header, type, sortable

#### Detail/Edit Pages

- Use `ItemDetailComponent` with `ItemDetailConfig`
- Example: User details, project details, client details
- Form fields: key, label, type, required, options
- Support create, update, delete operations

#### Dashboard Pages

- Use `DashboardComponent` with `DashboardConfig`
- Example: Analytics dashboard, client dashboard
- Widget types: counter, chart, table, list, heatmap, card

## Data Transfer Objects (DTOs)

### File Location

All DTOs go in `src/app/dto/`

### DTO Structure

```typescript
export interface UserDto {
  username: string;
  password: string;
  email: string;
  firstName: string;
  lastName: string;
  role: string;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
}
```

### Important Note on IDs

DTOs from backend do NOT have an id. The id is on the list item, not the DTO itself.

Use `QueryResult<T>` and `QueryResultItem<T>` from [src/app/components/query.dto.ts](mdc:src/app/components/query.dto.ts):

```typescript
export interface QueryResultItem<T> {
  item: T;
  id: string;
}

export interface QueryResult<T> {
  items: QueryResultItem<T>[];
  total: number;
  take: number;
  skip: number;
}
```

## Services

### File Location

- Services: `src/app/services/`
- Mock Services: `src/app/services-mock/`

### Service Pattern

```typescript
@Injectable({
  providedIn: "root",
})
export class AccountService {
  constructor(private backend: BackendService, private http: HttpClient) {}

  getAccounts(queryParams: QueryOptions): Observable<QueryResult<UserDto>> {
    return this.backend.getQuery<UserDto>("account", queryParams);
  }

  getAccount(id: string): Observable<UserDto> {
    return this.backend.get<UserDto>(`account/${id}`);
  }

  createAccount(user: UserDto): Observable<ProcessResult> {
    user.createdAt = undefined;
    user.updatedAt = undefined;
    return this.backend.post<ProcessResult>("account", user);
  }

  updateAccount(id: string, user: UserDto): Observable<ProcessResult> {
    return this.backend.put<ProcessResult>(`account/${id}`, user);
  }

  deleteAccount(id: string): Observable<ProcessResult> {
    return this.backend.delete<ProcessResult>(`account/${id}`);
  }
}
```

### Service Naming

- Use **singular** names (e.g., `AccountService`, not `AccountsService`)
- Backend endpoints are singular

### Mock Services

- Create mock services in `services-mock/` folder
- Name with `Mock` prefix (e.g., `MockAccountService`)
- Configure in `app.config.ts` for environment switching

